Diagnose the observed controller failure. Propose a concrete explanation, then directly edit the neural controller's weights or biases to compensate. You may evaluate at most 10 candidate patches. Do not train the network, compute gradients, or change the architecture or simulator. Prefer a small, explainable patch and preserve performance across varied starting states.

Start by looking at the weights and at one or more trajectories. When you are finished, reply without a tool call: state your diagnosis, what your best patch changes and why, and its measured scores.

